From 746f44902b038c908eb0420eab41aa27b3e2721b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gnanaprakash Elumalai <gelumala@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 25 Jun 2026 14:58:40 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] [PATCH] [prplMesh] 11k iPhone fixes, per-mode beacon
 duration,  steer_ire BTM detection, ACL persistence fix

1.Fix 11k beacon requests failing for iPhone clients: add mandatory SSID and
  Beacon Reporting Information subelements required by 802.11 spec. Without
  these, iPhones respond with an error report causing "Invalid 11k report
  length!" on the agent side.

2.Fix Active/Passive 11k scan mode silently failing for iPhones: check STA's
  RRM capabilities before sending the beacon request and fall back to Beacon
  Table mode if the STA does not support the requested scan mode. Steering app
  beacon requests are unaffected.

3.Add per-mode configurable 11k beacon measurement durations matching Prop
  defaults (Active=50 TU, Passive=110 TU, Table=200 TU). Previously the
  duration was hardcoded to 10 TU for all modes regardless of scan type.

4.Fix steer_ire CLI command using hardcoded BTM-capable assumption: query the
  STA's actual BTM support from the DB so that non-BTM STAs are correctly
  steered via legacy disassoc and their serving BSS is properly blocked.

5.Fix ACL persisting permanently after prplmesh restart: clear all DENY_ACL
  entries when the ap_manager reconnects to hostapd. TIMED_BLOCK ACLs survive
  a prplmesh-only restart (hostapd not restarted) but the controller's expiry
  timer is lost, leaving clients permanently blocked.

6.Restructure bml command bml_11k_query_trigger to remove duration field as
  1905 spec does not handle duration

7. controller: suppress RadioAdded storm on AP_AUTOCONFIG M1 re-send loop

dm_add_radio_element: fire RadioAdded only when a new DM instance is
created (radio.dm_path was empty). On subsequent M1 re-sends the radio
already has a dm_path, so RadioAdded is suppressed and only a DEBUG log
is emitted. This stops the ~100/min RadioAdded event storm observed in
CR4584267 where the ext agent's AP_AUTOCONFIGURATION FSM looped due to
timer overruns.

dm_set_device_ap_capabilities: always trigger Profile2ApCapability
vendor event regardless of whether R2APCapabilities DM writes succeeded.
On first M1 the Device.2.MultiAPDevice.R2APCapabilities sub-object may
not be instantiated yet (DM race), but consumers still need the
notification.

Signed-off-by: Gnanaprakash Elumalai <gelumala@qti.qualcomm.com>
